From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:50:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the S_UART0 pin group on
 PM3/PM4

The Radxa Cubie A7S routes PM3 and PM4 to pins 2 and 3 of its second
pin header, J6. S_UART0 can use them, but the SoC dtsi has only its
PL6/PL7 pin group.

Add the pin group for RX/TX on PM3/PM4. The two pins select S_UART0 with
different values: PM3 is S-UART0-RX with function 4, PM4 is S-UART0-TX
with function 2 (A733 manual, 18.14.3.1, table 18-39), so the group
gives one value per pin. The pins carry other functions as well, so a
board uses one function on them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: S_UART0 on PM3/PM4 loops data back with
pins 2 and 3 of J6 bridged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index f4069930b9db..17afe7687106 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1842,6 +1842,13 @@ r_uart0_pl6_pins: r-uart0-pl6-pins {
 				function = "s_uart0";
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_uart0_pm3_pins: r-uart0-pm3-pins {
+				pins = "PM3", "PM4";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <4>, <2>;
+				function = "s_uart0";
+			};
+
 			/omit-if-no-ref/
 			r_spi0_pl5_pins: r-spi0-pl5-pins {
 				pins = "PL5", "PL6", "PL7";
